<rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom" xmlns:media="http://search.yahoo.com/mrss/" xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/"><channel><title>NYT &gt; Technology</title><link>https://www.nytimes.com/section/technology</link><description>Technology industry news, commentary, and analysis, with reporting on big tech, startups, and internet culture. The New York Times is a hub for conversation about news and ideas.</description><atom:link rel="self" href="https://rss.nytimes.com/services/xml/rss/nyt/Technology.xml" type="application/rss+xml" /><item><title>I Gave My Life Over to Meta’s A.I. Agent and Was Blown Away</title><link>https://www.nytimes.com/2026/09/22/technology/meta-muse-ai-agent.html?partner=rss&amp;emc=rss</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.nytimes.com/2026/09/22/technology/meta-muse-ai-agent.html?partner=rss&amp;emc=rss</guid><atom:link rel="standout" href="https://www.nytimes.com/2026/09/22/technology/meta-muse-ai-agent.html?partner=rss&amp;emc=rss" /><description>Muse, Meta’s A.I. agent, helped handle my dental insurance, booked dinner reservations and created a podcast for me. It also required my most personal data, and trust.</description><dc:creator>Eli Tan</dc:creator><pubDate>Tue, 22 Sep 2026 15:55:03 GMT</pubDate><category domain="http://www.nytimes.com/namespaces/keywords/nyt_des">Artificial intelligence</category><category domain="http://www.nytimes.com/namespaces/keywords/nyt_des">Meta</category><category domain="http://www.nytimes.com/namespaces/keywords/nyt_des">Privacy</category><category domain="http://www.nytimes.com/namespaces/keywords/nyt_des">Computers and the Internet</category><category domain="http://www.nytimes.com/namespaces/keywords/nyt_des">Tech Industry</category><category domain="http://www.nytimes.com/namespaces/keywords/nyt_des">Mobile Apps</category><category domain="http://www.nytimes.com/namespaces/keywords/nyt_des">health insurance</category><media:content url="https://static01.nyt.com/images/2026/09/26/multimedia/META-MUSE-1-01-tlfz/META-MUSE-1-01-tlfz-videoSixteenByNineJumbo1600-v2.jpg" medium="image"><media:credit>Poppy Lynch for The New York Times</media:credit><media:description>The New York Times reporter Eli Tan using Meta Muse to buy movie tickets in San Francisco.</media:description></media:content></item><item><title>How to Listen to Your Favorite Music, Online or Off the Grid</title><link>https://www.nytimes.com/2026/09/30/technology/personaltech/how-to-listen-to-your-favorite-music-online-or-off-the-grid.html?partner=rss&amp;emc=rss</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.nytimes.com/2026/09/30/technology/personaltech/how-to-listen-to-your-favorite-music-online-or-off-the-grid.html?partner=rss&amp;emc=rss</guid><atom:link rel="standout" href="https://www.nytimes.com/2026/09/30/technology/personaltech/how-to-listen-to-your-favorite-music-online-or-off-the-grid.html?partner=rss&amp;emc=rss" /><description>Streaming services can introduce you to a wonderland of nearly unlimited audio, but downloading your digital collection has advantages.</description><dc:creator>J. D. Biersdorfer</dc:creator><pubDate>Wed, 30 Sep 2026 09:03:08 GMT</pubDate><category domain="http://www.nytimes.com/namespaces/keywords/nyt_des">iTunes</category><category domain="http://www.nytimes.com/namespaces/keywords/nyt_des">None</category><category domain="http://www.nytimes.com/namespaces/keywords/nyt_des">Android</category><category domain="http://www.nytimes.com/namespaces/keywords/nyt_des">Smartphone</category><category domain="http://www.nytimes.com/namespaces/keywords/nyt_des">Music</category><category domain="http://www.nytimes.com/namespaces/keywords/nyt_des">Audio Recordings</category><category domain="http://www.nytimes.com/namespaces/keywords/nyt_des">Downloads and Streaming</category><category domain="http://www.nytimes.com/namespaces/keywords/nyt_des">Mobile Apps</category><category domain="http://www.nytimes.com/namespaces/keywords/nyt_des">YouTube Music K