/nyt_des">Regulation and Deregulation</category><category domain="http://www.nytimes.com/namespaces/keywords/nyt_des">Russian American</category><category domain="http://www.nytimes.com/namespaces/keywords/nyt_des">Politics</category><category domain="http://www.nytimes.com/namespaces/keywords/nyt_des">Computers and the Internet</category><category domain="http://www.nytimes.com/namespaces/keywords/nyt_des">Tech Industry</category><media:content url="https://static01.nyt.com/images/2026/10/01/multimedia/01biz-Russia-AI-Songs-1-fmbg/01biz-Russia-AI-Songs-1-fmbg-videoSixteenByNineJumbo1600.jpg" medium="image"><media:credit>Nanna Heitmann for The New York Times</media:credit><media:description>Russian society is becoming increasingly militaristic since the war in Ukraine began. These soldiers marched in Moscow in a parade in 2023.</media:description></media:content></item><item><title>What’s Next for ‘Hard Fork’?</title><link>https://www.nytimes.com/2026/10/01/podcasts/hard-fork-whats-next.html?partner=rss&amp;emc=rss</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.nytimes.com/2026/10/01/podcasts/hard-fork-whats-next.html?partner=rss&amp;emc=rss</guid><atom:link rel="standout" href="https://www.nytimes.com/2026/10/01/podcasts/hard-fork-whats-next.html?partner=rss&amp;emc=rss" /><description>The podcast’s next chapter begins this week.</description><dc:creator>Max Read, Whitney Jones, Eddie Costas, Vjeran Pavic, Chris Wood, Marion Lozano and Rowan Niemisto</dc:creator><pubDate>Thu, 01 Oct 2026 11:00:22 GMT</pubDate><category domain="http://www.nytimes.com/namespaces/keywords/nyt_des">science</category><category domain="http://www.nytimes.com/namespaces/keywords/nyt_des">Artificial intelligence</category><category domain="http://www.nytimes.com/namespaces/keywords/nyt_des">Podcast</category><category domain="http://www.nytimes.com/namespaces/keywords/nyt_des">internal-open-access-audio</category><media:content url="https://static01.nyt.com/images/2026/10/01/podcasts/01hardfor